$CATEGORY: Odyssey2

::Q00::[markdown]When Telemachus calls the assembly, the first speaker is the father of Antiphus, who (we learn) was killed in the cave of the Cyclops. The agéd speaker's name is {=Aegyptius}.

::Q01::[markdown]Who says, to Telemachus, "Well, the big speaker, the mighty orator."? {=Antinous}

::Q02::[markdown]Penelope claimed to be weaving a shroud for {=Laertes}.

::Q03::[markdown]Penelope fooled the suitors with this weaving-ploy for how many years? {=three =3}

::Q04::[markdown]After Telemachus gets very forceful, Zeus sends two birds as an omen. What kind of birds? {=eagle =eagles}

::Q05::[markdown]And old friend of Odysseus speaks, a man whom Odysseus put in charge of all his house when he left with his ships. Not to be confused with "Mentes", this friend is {=Mentor}.

::Q06::[markdown]{=Leocritus}, Eveanor's son, actually threatens Odysseus with death, should he come home.

::Q07::[markdown]For his journey, Telemachus needs twelve jars of the best wine, and {=20 =twenty} quarts of ground barley meal. No need to suffer on a long journey! Wine won't go bad, like water might, and it is more fun. Barley is high-carb, if you are rowing from Ithaca to Pylos.

::Q08::[markdown]In a bronze-age Greek sailing ship, do you leave the main-mast upright when you aren't sailing it? {=no ~yes}